# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
"""erhai-lab: suspend/resume test lab for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai, SM8750).

One stdlib-only tool (eng review D4). Subcommands:

  fetch <candidate>   download a CI-built lab kernel, verify SHA256SUMS and the
                      UKI/modules kernelrelease, install it beside the package
                      kernel (/boot/<kver>.efi + /usr/lib/modules/<kver>/)
  arm / disarm        install / remove the one-attempt suspend override
                      (zz-erhai-lab.conf); outside an armed attempt the dev's
                      own suspend path runs untouched (D19)
  plan                print the hook step plan an attempt would run
  hook pre|post       called by systemd-sleep through the system-sleep caller
  probe               run one lab attempt (pm_test rungs E1-E4.5 in wave 1a)
  boot / ack          next-boot classifier and screen ack     (wave 1b)

One attempt:

  erhai-lab probe --rung E2 --wifi L1 --display park
    re-exec as a transient system unit (outside user.slice)       D20
    refuse: E0 / real-sleep rungs / no pm_test / not a lab kernel
    write /run/erhai-lab/attempt.json, set pm_test, arm the override D19
    systemctl suspend
      NetworkManager tears Wi-Fi down on PrepareForSleep            D15
      systemd-sleep -> hook pre, one ordered list, each step budgeted:
        display park|off, watcher stop, psoc timer freeze,
        [wifi settle, unbind L1 (, L2)], sync, journal, [alarm last]
        any failure -> pm_test=freezer, undo in reverse, abort      D7
      kernel: freeze -> devices -> (platform) -> back after pm_test_delay
      systemd-sleep -> hook post: readouts, resume-ok, undo, panel,
        evidence in /var/lib/erhai-sleep/<bootid>/<ts>/
    wait for the post hook, disarm, restore pm_test, print verdict

Records, rungs and classes are described in docs/ladder.md.
"""

